Package: statsalike
Type: Package
Title: 'Stata'-Style Tables, Summaries and Regressions for Data Frames
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R:
    person("Stefan", "Kirchner", email = "s.kirchner@fau.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides commands that reproduce the output of the 'Stata'
    commands describe, codebook, summarize, tabulate (including tab1, tab2
    and the options summarize and generate), table (in the syntax of 'Stata'
    17 and later), pwcorr, ttest, oneway, anova, alpha, regress, logit,
    probit, mlogit, ologit, oprobit, poisson, nbreg, tobit, margins,
    marginsplot, predict, estat, test, lincom, contrast, lrtest, linktest,
    lroc, lsens, avplot, cprplot and etable. The package is meant for users
    who move from 'Stata' to R or work with both and want familiar
    descriptive tables and routines without combining several packages. All
    functions that analyze data take a data frame as their first argument,
    so they work with pipes, and support tidy evaluation, grouping with
    group_by() from 'dplyr' (the equivalent of the by prefix in 'Stata'),
    frequency, analytic, importance and sampling weights, robust and
    cluster-robust standard errors, and value and variable labels from
    'haven'. Results are 'tibble' data frames that print in the layout of
    'Stata' output and can be exported to HTML and 'Word' (DOCX) files. The
    commands are an independent implementation in R that uses no 'Stata'
    code. Their output was compared automatically with that of 'Stata' 15.1.
    'Stata' is a registered trademark of StataCorp LLC. This package is not
    affiliated with or endorsed by StataCorp.
